<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI26-RBQA-F001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI26-RBQA-F001" ;
  triage:title "reconcile_peer constructs an independent RequestDeadline instead of consuming caller-admitted deadline" ;
  triage:description "ruthless-boundary-qa found during AICH-S6-QA-INTEGRITY-2 (PR #641 @ 584c4c176b7dab82945fb2463f59d06857e58ba2) that crates/atm-daemon/src/runtime_health/peer_sync.rs:41, function reconcile_peer, constructs its own independent RequestDeadline::after(Duration::from_secs(5)) rather than consuming/propagating the caller-admitted deadline passed through the request path. Additionally, dispatch_non_write discards the inbound deadline entirely for PeerSync requests. This is pre-existing on this branch (the file was not touched by AI.26's own diff) -- not new drift introduced by the ancestry replay -- but it is a real, currently-unfixed defect on the branch." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
